Hello everyone!

As July 2024 approaches, we're excited to update you on our progress toward the game's launch. Here’s what we’ve been up to:
[b]- Localization Efforts:[/b] We are localizing the game in Romanian, Lithuanian, Finnish, Russian, and Italian to make our game accessible to a wider audience. This step was possible with the support from our partners of the Erasmus+ project: ZURY Association - Romania, Euro - Net – Italy, VšĮ Robotikos mokykla – Lithuania and Vantaan Venäläinen Klubi ry – Finland;
[b]- Translation:[/b] We're translating all content to ensure every player enjoys a fully immersive experience;
[b]- Google Play Integration: [/b]Adapting the game for Android devices to ensure smooth gameplay across different platforms;
[b]- UI Testing: [/b]Our team is diligently testing the user interface to ensure it is intuitive and user-friendly;

Stay tuned for more updates as we gear up for the big day in July!

Hello everyone!

We're glad to share a peek into the steps of preparation of "SirKwitz," our educational game designed to make initiating in coding accessible and fun. Over the past months, our team has been dedicated to:
- refining the gameplay experience, ensuring each of the puzzles not only teaches core programming concepts but is also engaging and intuitive;
- testing extensively to guarantee that the user interface is clean and user-friendly – work in progress;
- making sure that our story-driven approach seamlessly integrates learning with fun;
- adjust the support areas based on the feedback we got from the first 10 testers;
- refining our tutorial system to make the learning curve smoother for beginners;
- adding more levels to expand the challenges and extend gameplay;
- enhancing graphics and animations to make our friendly robot and its environment more appealing;

Stay tuned for more updates!
